P1. Resolve on a flat four-marker set
=====================================

commutative + idempotent binary ops on 4 elements : 4096
of those, also associative (= join semilattices)  : 76

K1  Resolve(Hot, Precise) = Precise               : 31 survive
K2  and Resolve(Cold, Hot) != Hot   [I17]         : 24 survive
K3  and Resolve(Cold, Hot) != Cold  [I5]          : 9 survive

What K1-satisfying semilattices are FORCED to decide for Hot v Cold:
  Hot v Cold = Hot      : 7 of 31
  Hot v Cold = Warm     : 2 of 31
  Hot v Cold = Cold     : 15 of 31
  Hot v Cold = Precise  : 7 of 31

9 semilattice(s) satisfy all three. Each is listed with the partial
order it induces, so the reader can check it against the intents:

  --- survivor 1 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Warm
  Hot v Warm    = Warm
  Cold v Warm   = Warm
  Cold v Precise= Warm
  Warm v Precise= Warm
  order: Hot<=Warm, Hot<=Precise, Cold<=Warm, Precise<=Warm

  --- survivor 2 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Warm
  Cold v Warm   = Warm
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Warm
  order: Hot<=Warm, Hot<=Precise, Cold<=Warm, Cold<=Precise, Precise<=Warm

  --- survivor 3 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Warm
  Hot v Warm    = Warm
  Cold v Warm   = Warm
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Warm, Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Warm, Cold<=Precise

  --- survivor 4 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Precise
  Cold v Warm   = Warm
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Warm, Cold<=Precise

  --- survivor 5 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Hot
  Cold v Warm   = Cold
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Hot, Warm<=Cold, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Precise

  --- survivor 6 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Precise
  Cold v Warm   = Cold
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Cold, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Precise

  --- survivor 7 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Hot
  Cold v Warm   = Precise
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Hot, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Precise

  --- survivor 8 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Warm
  Cold v Warm   = Precise
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Warm, Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Precise

  --- survivor 9 ---
  Hot v Cold    = Precise
  Hot v Warm    = Precise
  Cold v Warm   = Precise
  Cold v Precise= Precise
  Warm v Precise= Precise
  order: Hot<=Precise, Warm<=Precise, Cold<=Precise

--- the same question on a PRODUCT of per-axis chains ---
elements in the product lattice        : 27
idempotence  holds on 27/27
commutativity holds on 729/729
associativity holds on 19683/19683

The product needs no order to be chosen: every pair has a join by
construction, so the four presets can be NAMED POINTS in it without
the resolution question ever arising as a separate design decision.
